    <string name="permissions_title">Permissions ICdetection needs</string>
    <string name="permission_location_title">Precise location</string>
    <string name="permission_location_body">Android only shares the serving and neighbour cells (Cell ID, PCI, frequency, signal) with apps that have location access. GPS coordinates also let the app compare each antenna with where it was seen before (H11, H13, H16), record where an incident happened and build the Geometry view. While monitoring runs, location is used continuously by a foreground service with a visible notification.</string>
    <string name="permission_phone_title">Phone state</string>
    <string name="permission_phone_body">Needed to follow the network state: operator, registration, service and data-network changes, and the cellular security events Android reports. ICdetection does not read calls, SMS, contacts, your phone number or IMEI.</string>
    <string name="permission_notifications_title">Notifications (optional)</string>
    <string name="permission_notifications_body">Shows the ongoing monitoring notification and warns you when an anomaly is confirmed. You can deny it: monitoring still works, but you will not see alerts outside the app.</string>
    <string name="permissions_privacy">Coordinates and radio readings are stored only on this phone. OpenCellID checks send the cell identity, never your position, and only if you add an API key in Settings.</string>
    <string name="permissions_denied_hint">If you denied a permission and Android no longer asks, grant it from the app settings.</string>
